        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 24 at 11:08AM AKDT until September 24 at 10:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southeast winds 35 to 45 mph with gusts up to 65 mph
expected. The strongest winds are expected near Togiak, with winds
gusting to 60 mph from Dillingham east.

* WHERE...Northern Bristol Bay Coast.

* WHEN...Until 10 PM AKDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects and a few
power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A strong front moving inland from the eastern
Bering will bring gusty southeasterly winds to the Southwest
coastline beginning this morning. Winds are expected to peak around
noon through 4pm AKDT today, then steadily diminish through this
evening.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind. Prepare for the possibility of widespread
power outages. Use caution if you must drive.</instruction>
